\maketitle

\noindent\textbf{What this document is.} An expansion of one derivation from the
paper named above, written so that every step is explicit and every step names
what licenses it. It is a companion to the paper, not a replacement for it, and
it proves nothing the paper did not.

\noindent\textbf{How to read a step.} Each block shows what the step starts from,
what it produces, and the name of the move between them. Underneath: what makes
the move legal, what would break it, what a mechanical checker made of it, and
the same idea in plain language.

\noindent\textbf{Where it stops.} A step that could not be made explicit appears
as a red block where it would have been, and again in the gap ledger at the end.
